<title>USA: US aluminum center shipments up 7.5 percent in Q1.</title>
<headline>US aluminum center shipments up 7.5 percent in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. service center shipments of aluminum mill products in the first quarter were 7.5 percent above the same period last year, the National Association of Aluminum Distributors said.</p>
<p>According to NAAD's three month moving average index, shipments in March rose to 146.1 points compared to 142.3 points in February. The inventory index rose to 129.1 points from 125.2 in February, and 131.2 in March 1996.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
